  "title": "Russell Westbrook Collected So Many Stats, He Broke Them",
  "subtitle": null,
  "byline": null,
  "publishedAt": null,
  "contentHtml": "<figure><a href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/%24s_!QP6s!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fdb971218-e4ec-4cc7-859a-e9ef5867bba2_1448x1086.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n<img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/%24s_!QP6s!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fdb971218-e4ec-4cc7-859a-e9ef5867bba2_1448x1086.png\" width=\"1448\" height=\"1086\" data-size=\"normal\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n\n</a><figcaption><strong>Russell Westbrook.</strong> (Based on <strong><a href=\"https://www.gettyimages.com/detail/news-photo/russell-westbrook-of-the-oklahoma-city-thunder-goes-to-the-news-photo/888030780?slot=47&amp;adppopup=true\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">the original </a></strong>by Joe Murphy/NBAE via Getty Images)</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Russell Westbrook’s <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/49592048/russell-westbrook-announces-nba-retirement-18-seasons\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">retirement last week</a> was an occasion to be nostalgic for the peak of one of basketball’s <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nba/story/_/id/49593121/russell-westbrook-retires-nba-legacy-triple-double-records-durant-partnership\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">most electrifying players</a> — a relentless 6-foot-4 wrecking ball of pure kinetic energy, who played every possession as if the opposing team had personally insulted him.</p>\n<p>But for me, it was also an occasion to revisit Westbrook’s complicated relationship with the statistical record book. It was through numbers that we came to define his greatness, even as Westbrook spent his career changing what they meant — and exposing their limitations.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/subscribe?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p>\n<p>One of Westbrook’s lasting legacies as an NBA player will come down to two words:</p>\n<p>Nobody was better at breaking double-digits in the point, rebound and assist columns<a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/#footnote-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1</a> than Russ, who retires as the NBA’s all-time leader in <a href=\"https://www.basketball-reference.com/leaders/trp_dbl_season.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">single-season</a> and <a href=\"https://www.basketball-reference.com/leaders/trp_dbl_career.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">career triple-doubles</a> after having long since surpassed Oscar Robertson in both categories:</p>\n<p>\n          <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/russell-westbrook-collected-so-many\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n              Read more\n          </a>\n      </p>",
